@startuml

title Access Token: how a service decides whether to serve a request


start
:a request arrives;
if (an Authorization or\nX-Delegated-Authorization header?) then (no)
  :reply X-Error: unauthorized;
  stop
endif
if (the signature verifies with\nIAM's public key?) then (no)
  :reply X-Error: unauthorized;
  stop
endif
if (the token has expired?) then (yes)
  :reply X-Error: token_expired;
  note right: the only refusal a caller\nmay retry, after a renewal
  stop
endif
:build the request context:\nthe delegated identity if present,\nelse the direct one;
if (the context holds the\noperation's permission?) then (no)
  :reply X-Error: forbidden;
  stop
endif
:set the tenant and the party\non the database session;
:serve the request;
note right: row-level security now\nfilters every read
stop
@enduml
